# 📄 Chat Module SRS (Software Requirements Specification)

## 1. Overview

This document defines the architecture, data models, APIs, and real-time communication design for a **multi-platform chat system** supporting:

* Web (React)
* Mobile (Flutter - iOS & Android)

The system is designed for:

* 1–1 chats (support chats)
* Group chats (orders, quotes, disputes)
* Dynamic participant roles
* Chat transfer and conversion between contexts

---

## 2. System Architecture

### 2.1 High-Level Components

* **Frontend (Web):** React
* **Mobile Apps:** Flutter (iOS & Android)
* **Backend:** Node.js (Express)
* **Database:** MongoDB
* **Real-time Layer:** WebSockets (Socket.IO)
* **File Storage:** S3 / Cloudinary
* **Push Notifications:** Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)

---

### 2.2 Communication Layers

#### REST APIs

Used for:

* Authentication
* Chat creation
* Message history
* File uploads
* Chat updates (transfer, conversion)

#### WebSockets

Used for:

* Real-time messaging
* Typing indicators
* Read receipts
* Chat updates (assignment, role changes)

---

## 3. Core Concepts

### 3.1 Unified Chat Model

All chat types are stored in a **single collection**.

#### Chat Schema

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  type: "support" | "order" | "quote" | "dispute",
  isGroup: Boolean,

  participants: [userId],

  roles: [
    {
      userId: ObjectId,
      role: "customer" | "employee" | "admin" | "partner"
    }
  ],

  context: {
    orderId: ObjectId | null,
    quoteId: ObjectId | null,
    disputeId: ObjectId | null
  },

  assignedTo: ObjectId | null,

  status: "open" | "closed" | "pending",

  linkedChats: [chatId],

  lastMessage: Object,
  updatedAt: Date,
  createdAt: Date
}
```

---

### 3.2 Message Schema

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  chatId: ObjectId,
  senderId: ObjectId,

  type: "text" | "file" | "image" | "system",

  content: String,
  fileUrl: String,

  metadata: Object,

  createdAt: Date
}
```

---

### 3.3 Read Tracking

```
{
  userId: ObjectId,
  chatId: ObjectId,
  lastReadAt: Date
}
```

---

## 4. Chat Types

### 4.1 Support Chat (1–1 Dynamic)

* User remains constant
* Assigned employee can change
* Uses `assignedTo` field

---

### 4.2 Group Chats

Used for:

* Orders
* Quotes
* Disputes

Participants may include:

* Customer
* Employee
* Admin
* Partner

---

## 5. Chat Transfer & Conversion

### 5.1 Reassignment (Same Chat)

```
assignedTo = newEmployeeId
```

* No message movement
* History preserved

---

### 5.2 Context Conversion

Example:
Support → Order

```
chat.type = "order"
chat.context.orderId = "123"
```

---

### 5.3 Chat Linking

```
linkedChats: [chatId]
```

Used to associate related conversations without merging them.

---

### 5.4 System Messages

Used for audit trail:

```
{
  type: "system",
  content: "Chat transferred to Employee X"
}
```

---

## 6. Real-Time Design

### 6.1 Connection

* Clients connect using JWT authentication
* Each user joins:

  * Personal room → `userId`
  * Chat rooms → `chatId`

---

### 6.2 Core Events

#### Client → Server

* `send_message`
* `join_chat`
* `leave_chat`
* `typing`
* `read_messages`

#### Server → Client

* `receive_message`
* `new_chat`
* `chat_assigned`
* `member_added`
* `member_removed`
* `chat_updated`

---

### 6.3 Message Flow

1. Client emits `send_message`
2. Server saves message
3. Server emits to `chatId` room

---

## 7. File Sharing

### Flow:

1. Client requests upload URL
2. Uploads file to storage (S3/Cloudinary)
3. Sends file URL in message

---

## 8. API Design

### 8.1 Create Chat

```
POST /chats
```

---

### 8.2 Get Messages

```
GET /messages?chatId=123&after=timestamp
```

---

### 8.3 Transfer Chat

```
POST /chats/:id/transfer
```

---

### 8.4 Convert Chat Type

```
POST /chats/:id/convert
```

---

### 8.5 Add/Remove Members

```
POST /chats/:id/members
DELETE /chats/:id/members/:userId
```

---

## 9. Push Notifications

Used when users are offline.

### Trigger:

* New message
* Assignment changes
* Group updates

---

## 10. Permissions (RBAC)

Role-based access:

| Role     | Permissions           |
| -------- | --------------------- |
| Customer | Send/receive messages |
| Employee | Respond, manage chats |
| Admin    | Full control          |
| Partner  | Respond   |

---

## 11. Scalability Considerations

* Use Redis for WebSocket scaling
* Index MongoDB:

  * `chatId + createdAt`
  * `participants`
* Paginate messages
* Avoid embedding messages in chat documents

---

## 12. Error Handling & Reliability

* Handle socket reconnections
* Sync missed messages via API
* Ensure idempotent message handling
* Retry failed uploads

---

## 13. Security

* JWT authentication (REST + sockets)
* Validate inputs
* Rate limit messages
* Secure file uploads

---

## 14. MVP Scope

### Phase 1

* 1–1 support chat
* Real-time messaging
* Basic UI (React)

### Phase 2

* Group chats
* Flutter integration
* File sharing

### Phase 3

* Push notifications
* Read receipts
* Chat transfer & conversion

---

## 15. Future Enhancements

* Chat queues & auto-assignment
* SLA tracking
* Analytics & reporting
* Message search
* Reactions & replies

---

## 16. Key Design Principles

* Single chat model for all types
* Role-based permissions (not hardcoded logic)
* Context-driven chat meaning
* No message duplication
* Real-time + fallback sync via APIs

---

## 17. Summary

This system is designed as a **scalable, multi-platform communication layer** supporting:

* Dynamic participant management
* Business-context chats (orders, disputes, etc.)
* Real-time and offline communication
* Extensibility for future enterprise features

---

**End of Document**




