# 📄 Chat Module – Phase-wise Implementation Plan (SRS Addendum)

---

## 1. Purpose

This document breaks down the chat system into **clear implementation phases**, allowing incremental development, testing, and scaling across:

* React (Web)
* Flutter (iOS & Android)
* Express (Backend)
* MongoDB (Database)

Each phase is **independently deliverable** and builds toward a production-grade system.

---

# 🧩 Phase 0 – Foundation Setup

## Objective

Prepare core infrastructure and baseline project structure.

## Scope

* Backend project setup (Express)
* MongoDB connection
* Basic folder structure
* Environment configuration
* Logging & error handling

## Deliverables

* Running backend server
* DB connection established
* Base project structure

## Notes

* No chat functionality yet
* Prepare for modular architecture

---

# 🧩 Phase 1 – Authentication & User System

## Objective

Enable secure user access across platforms.

## Features

* User registration/login
* JWT authentication
* Role assignment (customer, employee, admin, partner)

## APIs

* `POST /auth/login`
* `POST /auth/register`
* `GET /me`

## Deliverables

* Auth working in React
* Token-based access control

## Dependencies

* Required for all future phases

---

# 🧩 Phase 2 – Basic 1–1 Chat (Support Chat MVP)

## Objective

Implement core messaging between a user and an assigned employee.

## Features

* Create support chat
* Assign employee (`assignedTo`)
* Send/receive messages (real-time)
* Message persistence
* Basic chat UI (React)

## Data

* Chat model (type: "support")
* Message model

## Real-Time

Use WebSockets via Socket.IO:

* `send_message`
* `receive_message`

## Deliverables

* Working 1–1 chat (web)
* Messages stored in DB

## Notes

* No Flutter yet
* No file sharing

---

# 🧩 Phase 3 – Message History & Sync

## Objective

Ensure reliability for offline users.

## Features

* Fetch message history
* Incremental sync (`after` timestamp)
* Pagination

## APIs

* `GET /messages?chatId=&after=`

## Deliverables

* Reload-safe chat
* Backend sync logic

## Importance

* Critical for Flutter/mobile support later

---

# 🧩 Phase 4 – Flutter Integration

## Objective

Extend chat functionality to mobile apps.

## Features

* Socket connection in Flutter
* JWT-based socket auth
* Message send/receive
* Sync missed messages

## Deliverables

* Chat working in Flutter (iOS & Android)
* Same backend used

## Notes

* Maintain shared event contract

---

# 🧩 Phase 5 – File & Media Sharing

## Objective

Enable file/image messaging across platforms.

## Features

* File upload via backend (signed URLs)
* Storage integration (S3/Cloudinary)
* Send file messages

## Message Update

```js
type: "file" | "image"
fileUrl: String
```

## Deliverables

* File sharing in React & Flutter

## Notes

* Do NOT store files in MongoDB

---

# 🧩 Phase 6 – Group Chats

## Objective

Support multi-user conversations.

## Features

* Create group chat
* Add/remove members
* Roles per user
* Group messaging

## Chat Update

```js
isGroup: true
roles: [{ userId, role }]
```

## Real-Time

* Room-based messaging (`chatId`)

## Deliverables

* Group chat functional (web + mobile)

---

# 🧩 Phase 7 – Roles & Permissions (RBAC)

## Objective

Control access based on user roles.

## Roles

* Customer
* Employee
* Admin
* Partner

